proof.text:
Apply [lem-per-lisse-completed-system-comparison] on each Noetherian separated $T_
u$. The lattice $L_
u$ determines normalized finite locally free etale sheaves $L_{
u,n}$ over $A/\varpi^n$, with $L_{
u,n+1}\otimes_{A/\varpi^{n+1}}A/\varpi^n\simeq L_{
u,n}$ and $L_
u\simeq\varprojlim_n
u^*L_{
u,n}$. Thus $(L_{
u,n})_n$, after inverting $\varpi$ and including $E$ into $\Qlb$, is exactly a classical lisse $\Qlb$-sheaf under [def-pod-lisse-l-adic-sheaves]. In particular the reductions are ordinary quotients of a lisse lattice; no concentration assertion is being made for the derived reduction of a torsion integral representative of $M$.

